# Architecture

- Dependency flow is browser → BFF → domain/Platform. Browser code never calls Platform.
- `apps/web` may use browser contracts and public config; it must not import `@brand/platform`, Platform wire types, or server-only config.
- Browser-facing schemas belong in `packages/contracts`.
- Use cases and Platform-to-brand mapping belong in `packages/domain`.
- Platform transport, signing, endpoints, and wire types belong in `packages/platform`.
- Verify actual Platform contracts. Never invent endpoints, fields, or unsupported behavior.
- Never add EveryMatrix, `platformSource`, brand branching, legacy DTOs, or a CMS casino catalog unless explicitly requested.
- Cosmoswin and Betfinal are technical references for known contracts only.
- Casino, Live Casino, and Sportsbook are the core product.
- Prefer direct, maintainable code over speculative abstractions.
